A resolution: the game drawn at a share of the screen's resolution and stretched to fill it.

Joe, 2026-11-19: the in-game settings' Resolution, the screen's own or 80, 60 or 50 percent of it
(PocketResolution). The game is told a window, and a screen, that share of the host's size at the
screen's own density: it renders that share of the pixels each way, smoother and lighter on the
battery, softer to look at, and does not know the screen is larger. Its picture is stretched to
fill the host through a layer of its own, and touches are scaled by the same share on their way to
it, so a tap lands where it is drawn. A change applies at once, as a resize.
Upstream note: a general render resolution for guests; the settings that set it are Brighter Pocket's.

